==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Dragon King Vars''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''God-Emperor Vars''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Vars is a reliable backliner in general. His anti-Dark ability is also a nice addition. Despite Bombercat doing the job much better, Vars' range advantage allows him to hit Dark enemies that have few knockbacks and/or high range, as in the case with [[Le'noir]], [[Razorback]] and [[Casaurian Darkjo]], impeding them with his knockback ability if it does activate. His slow ability is universally useful, as his DPS, while decent, tends not to kill aggressive Black pushers easily. Though he does require proper support and therefore won't work alone, Vars does make the job much easier for your specialists like [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza]].

==='''True Form'''===
God-Emperor Vars gains increased health, damage and range. The stat boosts simply improve his general uses and while the minor range bonus may seem insignificant, Vars can now outrange certain backliners like [[Master A.]] and [[THE SLOTH]] (451/450 < 460), making him useful against them if you lack options.

==='''Talents'''===
Vars' [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] target talent and Curse Immunity are surprisingly useful, given many Relics have similarly long range and can be difficult to ward off with brute force alone due to their very high stats. His 460 range makes him useful against pushers like [[Relic Bun-Bun]], [[M. Ost]] and backliners like [[Othom]], as he can stay out of their range and consistently hinder their advance.

On the other hand, Vars' remaining talents are not as useful. Although Vars does have decent stats, Catseyes are better at boosting them, and his [[Knockback]] ability's 50% chance is already sufficient for what he does.

==='''Ultra Talents'''===
Do not invest in Vars's Ultra Talents.

What appears to be the main appeal of his kit is '''Attack Frequency Up''', which significantly increases his DPS and his pushing power, giving him near perfect uptime with his [[Slow]]. However, even with this Ultra Talent fully maxxed out, there is really no point investing into Vars as either a generalist attacker or an Anti-Dark/Relic crowd controller.

The most immediate rival for Vars is [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Esoteric Uril]], who does not require investing hundreds of NP to obtain and who also targets a more valuable trait in Aku. While it is true that getting Esoteric Uril requires you to clear the Infernal Tower, Vars with Target Relic and Curse Immune is already able to fight off against the important boss floors like Floor 50, so there's not really much justification for getting this Talent. On the anti-Dark side, [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]] is not only faster than Vars, but is also able to freeze his opponents. While some Dark enemies with Freeze Immunity do exist, units like [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]], [[Dark Lazer]] and [[Cats in a Box (Special Cat)|Heavy Assault C.A.T]] are so incredibly strong that you can just kill them with brute force instead of relying on Vars's Slow. For this reason, don't bother investing in '''Slow''' either.

On the generalist attacker side, Vars is still inferior to other Ubers with better generalist capabilities who make for better Dark Catseye investments like [[Dioramos (Uber Rare Cat)|Ascendant Dioramos]], or even other Ubers who don't need Dark Catseye investment at all like [[Baby Gao (Uber Rare Cat)|Mighty Lord Gao.]] While this Talent might make him a better generalist than [[Urs & Fenrir (Special Cat)|Awakened Urs]], it doesn't make him better than other Ubers by a long shot.

Finally, Vars gets '''[[Immune to Waves|Wave Immunity]]''' to gain better matchups against enemies like [[Gigahaniwan]], [[Masked Grandmaster Cat (Enemy)|Masked Grandmaster Cat]], [[Two Can]], and other general Wave enemies like [[Bore Jr.]]. Given how outclassed Vars is at the point in time where you are considering to purchase Ultra Talents, there is little value gained by purchasing his Talent both on the offensive side and to improve his matchups.

