==Trivia==
*Prior to [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]], Vars was a part of two other [[Cat Combo]]s: [[Valorous (Removed Combo)|Valorous]] and [[Dragon Emperors (Removed Combo)|Dragon Emperors]].
*Unlike other units in his [[Lords of Destruction DRAGON EMPERORS (Gacha Event)|respective set]], Vars is not a dragon - rather, Vars is the knight saddling on an unnamed dragon and attacks in place of it.
*In [[Nyanko Ecology Report Special Edition]], it was revealed that Vars's name is a reference to "Balus", the spell of destruction in the Studio Ghibli movie ''[[wikipedia:Castle in the Sky|Castle in the Sky]]'', itself derived from the Turkish word ''barış'' (meaning "peace"). The reference is much more obvious in Japanese, in which both ''Vars'' and ''Balus'' are written as バルス (''Barusu'').
*His choice of weapon may be a reference to the [[wikia:finalfantasy:Wind drake|wyvern]]-riding [[wikia:finalfantasy:Dragoon|Dragoons]] in ''[[wikipedia:Final Fantasy|Final Fantasy]]'', who fight using spears and lances. In [[Nyanko Daisensou|BCJP]], Vars's name also includes the Japanese name of the Dragoon class, "Dragon Knight" (竜騎士).
*Dragon King Vars's mount closely resembles a [[wikia:monsterhunter:Diablos|Diablos]] from the ''Monster Hunter'' series, while [[Skull Rider Vars (Uber Rare Cat)|Nightmare King Vars]]'s could be inspired by the [[wikia:monsterhunter:Black Diablos|Black Diablos]] subspecies.
*The verb "rode" in Vars' description is in the wrong tense: it is in the simple past tense when it is supposed to be in the present perfect tense ("ridden").

